Well, another no real conduct games and cute tricks. Well, only one 
cute trick this time. I used a twohanded sword for my main weapon. I 
played this on Nethack.alt.org

The RNG gave me a Lawful dwarven Valk for this game. My con was not 
high so I started the game with no intention of gaining levels for a 
while. I  wasn't dead set on the racket though. I let Maus kill most 
things but newts I wanted for myself. Not one gave me a buzz. 

The second level had a huge scroll shop and I priced I.D until I 
found identify. Nothing needed to be i.d.ed right away so I just left 
everything there. At some point around here I found an uncursed 
amulet and changed into a male. Most of the game was spent in this 
gender. 

We cleared our way down to the oracle on lvl 5, and it was then that 
I decided to go for a pure racket. (after increasing my hp to 20 with 
a !oH and finding a cloak of displacment.) On lvl 6 there was a 
problem with a trap door and we found a general store and a bones 
file. (I think) It wasn't too tough and we went back up to sokobon. 
Got refection and some more pets. Liepling, rugrat and Spatz. They 
didn't live very long.


The first level of the mines had a saddle. Left it there for now. 

Went down into mine town with around 9,000 zorkmids. Being a dwarf 
and having displacement made this trip easy. I ended up with 14 
points of protection! I usually can get 10, but this was unbelievable 
to me. I did my best to kill myself off at his point but having -23 
ac (I was wearing platemail) kept me alive. 

My first mistake was kicking down a locked door. It turned out to be 
a shop and I had locked this door. (doh!) my insane Ac for this stage 
of the game let me survive the encounter with the pissed of 
shopkeeper in spite of only being a puny first level valk. I ran like 
hell and displacement allowed my to get away. 
I immediately ran up the next level. I started killing stuff until I 
gain two levels and went back into minetown. 

I basically danced around doing all the mundane stuff people usually 
do in minetown except I had a pissed off shopkeeper running around 
trying to kill me. Kept things exciting.  I finally left minetown 
with exp level 6 and having dipped for Excalibur. The watch captain 
almost did me in, but I just danced him to death. I would wait until 
he got next to me, I would swing once, and then walk away. Without 
displacement and the 14 poins of protection this wouldn't have 
worked. 

Only Liepling and Rugrat survived this far. We went and got the luck 
stone. I found one polytrap and upgraded rugrat to an Olog-hai and 
Liepling into a Silver Dragon. I hit and polymorphed into a nymph. I 
still was killing things left and right, so kept the form for awhile. 

We came back to minetown and Rugrat and Liepling killed all the 
shopkeepers for me. Finally, no more monkeys on my back. I dontated 
and received some more protection. (I ended up with 17 points 
eventually, because my first two prayers gained protection as well.) 

I don't really remember the next stage of the game except that is was 
absurdly easy. I do remember riding Liepling as soon as we got into 
the main dungeon. It was pretty much hack and slash. 

Lvl 11 had the portal to the quest and  an altar and sink.  Lvl 10 
also had an altar and sink. I made my stash there. I also put my 
three wands of polymorph into my stash. I wasn't quite ready for 
inventory management just yet. I also started collecting stuff for my 
eventual metamorphose into a spellcaster. 

Lvl 13 had the portal to fort Knox. Killed everything but no grey 
dragon. There was a Death star and I gained disintegration resistance 
from it. Pulled all the junk into four piles and went to get my wand 
of poly. I found so many poly wands that I didn't bother combining 
the stashes. I polyed the armor in the fort and then went and polyed 
my stash for extra spellbooks and tools. (I had collected all tools I 
found so far.) I made all magical boots except speed and made all the 
mundane tools I wanted. Put on some lenses and read any spellbook 
that was lvl 3 or less. I replaced my armor with mithril so I still 
didn't convert to spellcaster mode. I replaced my gloves with GoP.  I 
also made about 3 two handed swords . I stashed Excalibur and 
enchanted my two handed sword up to +6. I used that for the rest of 
the game. 

I got crowned next and that rustproofed my weapon. I didn't bother 
with enchanting armor just yet because I wasn't wearing anything that 
I would keep until the end. I did enchant my Hawaiian shirt though.  
Nothing exciting happened on the road to medusa. Once I reached 
medusa, this didn't change. I normally dig down and come up to save 
time, but since I was riding a silver dragon I just went over and 
whacked her. 

I discovered something new at this point. I was invisible but 
Liepling was not. Even though the game turns both you and the mount 
invisible for display purposes, the game still treats both of you 
different. The first gaze attack was directed toward me, but the 
second one was directed toward Liepling and Medusa was stoned.  I 
nearly fell out of my seat laughing. 

I still didn't have MR and I was  getting nervous  because of this. 
As far as I was concerned I was still killable. I would have 
genocided L's but I still hadn't found any scrolls of genocide. I was 
hesitant in going to the castle level but I had telepathy and a wand 
of fire. If a Major Lich showed up, I had ways to defend myself. I 
went down and completely forgot what I was doing. I walked a few 
spaces without blinding myself and sure enough a master lich comes 
and attacks me. 

I was lucky. I engraved Elbereth and went to the stairs. The Lich 
only came next to me once more on the way back to the stairs and 
nothing bad happened. Once I got to the stairs I engraved again and 
whacked it to death with my two handed sword. 

We cleared the castle and I found nothing new. I put all tools and 
magical armor in my bag and used one wish A.S.A.P for blessed greased 
+3 dragon scale mail. Whew. 

The next phase was upgrade and stash management. I lost my protection 
(NOOOOO!) due to a gremlin attack somewhere, so I took the time to 
convert myself and get 10 points from the Valley of  the dead priest. 
(yes ten. I was getting lucky with this donating stuff. Also I found 
something strange. My first donation got me more than 1 point. How 
was this possible? Was it the conversion or the gremlin taking away 
my protection that fooled the gods?)   I used 3 wishes on magic 
markers and all those markers to write scrolls of charging.  Any 
charging scroll not used to enchant a marker was used on me. I was 
about exp lvl 15 at this point but only had around 16 spell points. 
Low wisdom, intelligence valk dwarf really get screwed in the spell 
point department. Well, I fixed that. I had about 280 when I was done 
with the scrolls. (confused blessed charging,baby!) I switched myself 
to spell casting mode. I had Magic missile, healing, and extra 
healing as the useful spells that I used often. Remove curse and 
Stone to flesh were also nice. 

I Next took and alchemized  7 !oFH into Gain ability and maxed out my 
intelligence and wisdom. I was still hoping for a helm of brilliance 
through poly, so I saved my last two wishes for later. I had Mmisile 
at 0% fail, so that was good enough for me. My inventory was +3 GDSM,  
+3 robe, leather gloves,+5 speedboots,  +5hawaiin shirt and leather 
helmet.  I didn't feel the need to write any ?oEA. My ac was good 
enough. 

The quest was a cake walk , but I got pretty tired of lugging around 
the orb of weight. The only reason I kept it was because I still had 
not found any unholy water so I had no way of cursing ?oT. I got 
tired of lugging around rug rat so I ditched him while I went pudding 
farming for spellbooks. I then went and Level teleported to the 
bottom of hell. I like to work my way up when exploring hell. I was 
able to finally cast magic mapping during this trip, but it got too 
faint to read. I cleared the wiz toward except for Rodney himself, 
and went back up for more messing around. I also sat on magic traps 
to get more loot and to recharge my spell points. 

I went back and forth with level teleports to visit a few lady demon 
friends of mine, but this life of debauchery and mayhem was starting 
to be too much of a pain. I just wanted to get the amulet back to the 
gods and go on vacation. I stopped at exp lvl 27 (as good as it 
gets.), wished for the helm of brilliance and a magic marker, and 
went down to kick some wizard and priest butt.  Liepling died many 
times but I raised him from the dead and retamed him if necessary.  
Mapping was at 50 something failure rate and detect  treasure at 23%. 
All unskilled  third level spells were at 0% failure. I could even 
cast the finger at 70% +3-8. I had two wands of death but I did use 
the finger several times in the sanctum. 

Anyways, I got the book and the amulet ASAP. I charmed every 
purpleworm that came my way and let one of them eat all the wraiths 
in the sanctum. Going back up was easy as a chaotic, and the few 
times I was thrown back the levels had stairs next to each other. 

When I hit my stash again I tamed rug rat and some random angel. I 
enchanted excalibur to +7 and gave it to the angel. Rugrat got to use 
Orcrist. I had two purple worms as well. Liepling finally ate a 
shapechanger corpse, so I replaced him with a red dragon. 

They only thing I needed for spells was magic missile and charm 
monster. I just memorized charm monster less than 1000 turns before 
so I only took Magic missile with me in the bag of holding. I ditched 
the orb of weight and made sure I had plenty of escape wands. I also 
switched my boots of speed for boots of jumping. I used up all my 
power on the haste spell. (all 345 of it.)

Earth didn't start off well. A Deathstar got both Rugrat and my new 
mount on the first turn there. Fire and Air were easy. I just ran for 
the portal and charmed things left and right. I forgot to whistle my 
pets before water so was left all alone until astral. 

Astral was also easy. I went to all three altars before I found the 
right one. Placed a Helm of opposite alignment on and offered the 
amulet.  I had about 20 pets at this point but since none of them 
were any of the ones I cared about I didn't bother bringing them with 
me.  

